Opt-in NVTX ranges on the vLLM engine step for Nsight Systems profiles
(docs/waste-profiling.md). With VLLM_APERTUS_NVTX=1 the worker module installs
apertus_bench.vllm_nvtx, which wraps the scheduler, the model runner (v2), the
rejection sampler and the DSpark/DFlash/EAGLE speculators in NVTX ranges. The
wrapping happens at run time, so this overlay touches only gpu_worker.py and
composes with the scheduler patches that edit model_runner.py and the
speculators. Without the variable it does nothing. serving/node-sweep.sh adds
it when the spec has a profiled arm.

--- a/workspace/vllm/vllm/v1/worker/gpu_worker.py
+++ b/workspace/vllm/vllm/v1/worker/gpu_worker.py
@@ -1320,3 +1320,13 @@
     # Init ec connector here before KV caches init
     # NOTE: We do not init KV caches for Encoder-only instance in EPD disagg mode
     ensure_ec_transfer_initialized(vllm_config)
+
+
+# Apertus (serving/patches/vllm-apertus-nvtx.patch): opt-in NVTX ranges on the
+# engine step for Nsight Systems profiles. The ranges live in the bench repo
+# (apertus_bench.vllm_nvtx, on the arm's PYTHONPATH) and wrap methods rather
+# than edit them, so this overlay composes with the scheduler patches.
+if os.environ.get("VLLM_APERTUS_NVTX") == "1":
+    from apertus_bench.vllm_nvtx import install as _apertus_nvtx_install
+
+    _apertus_nvtx_install()
